judge_raw_output:
The population has clearly shifted toward extreme, high-distance/high-spread designs while performance collapsed (mean performance 0.008636 vs 0.079682 in the previous iteration) — this points to an objective-weighting problem. I therefore propose reducing the weight on distance_from_center to restore exploitative pressure on performance.

